# Every path is the app.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves files, and only `/` exists as one. `/invite/<token>`,
# `/stats` and every other route belong to the router, which cannot run until
# something has been served — so without this, opening one directly is a 404.
#
# The invite link is the case that makes it not optional: it is the one URL
# somebody arrives at from outside, pasted into a browser, never navigated to
# from inside the app.
#
# 200 and not 302: the address stays what the person opened, which is what the
# router reads to decide where they landed.
/*    /index.html   200
